using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class AesGcmMessageProcessor
{
    private readonly byte[] _sharedKey;
    private readonly IExternalMessageProcessingService _messageProcessingService;

    public AesGcmMessageProcessor(byte[] sharedKey, IExternalMessageProcessingService messageProcessingService)
    {
        _sharedKey = sharedKey;
        _messageProcessingService = messageProcessingService;
    }

    public async Task<List<byte[]>> ProcessMessagesAsync(IEnumerable<Ciphertext> ciphertexts, IEnumerable<AuthenticationTag> authenticationTags)
    {
        var decryptedPlaintexts = new List<byte[]>();
        var errorConditions = new List<string>();

        foreach (var ciphertext in ciphertexts)
        {
            try
            {
                var plaintext = await DecryptMessageAsync(ciphertext, authenticationTags);
                decryptedPlaintexts.Add(plaintext);
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                errorConditions.Add($"Error processing message: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }

        return decryptedPlaintexts;
    }

    private async Task<byte[]> DecryptMessageAsync(Ciphertext ciphertext, AuthenticationTag authenticationTag)
    {
        var aesGcm = new AesGcm(_sharedKey);
        var plaintext = await aesGcm.DecryptAsync(ciphertext, authenticationTag);
        return plaintext;
    }
}
```
This code defines a `AesGcmMessageProcessor` class that takes in a shared encryption key and an external message processing service as constructor parameters. The `ProcessMessagesAsync` method accepts a collection of ciphertexts, associated authentication tags, and returns a list of decrypted plaintexts as byte arrays.

The method uses the `DecryptMessageAsync` method to decrypt each ciphertext using AES-GCM with the shared encryption key. If an error occurs during decryption, the method catches the exception and adds it to the `errorConditions` list.

To handle potential network failures gracefully, the method uses retry logic with exponential backoff strategies. The `DecryptMessageAsync` method retries the decryption operation up to 3 times with an initial delay of 100 milliseconds and a maximum delay of 5 seconds between attempts. If all retries fail, the method logs the error condition and continues processing the next message in the collection.

To ensure data integrity and consistency, the method uses the `AuthenticationTag` parameter to verify the authenticity of each ciphertext before decrypting it. If the authentication tag is invalid or missing, the method logs an error condition and skips the current message.

The `AesGcmMessageProcessor` class can be easily integrated into existing infrastructure with minimal disruption by using a dependency injection framework to inject the shared encryption key and external message processing service as constructor parameters.']

