The library does not accept any arguments or return any values. Instead, it provides a set of functions that can be used to encrypt, decrypt, generate digests, and sign/verify data using the various cryptographic algorithms supported by OpenSSL. These functions are designed to be thread-safe and optimized for performance under high-load conditions.

The library also includes comprehensive logging and error handling mechanisms to facilitate debugging and maintenance. When an error occurs during encryption or decryption, a log message is generated indicating the specific error that occurred. Similarly, when an error occurs during digest generation or signature verification, a log message is generated indicating the specific error that occurred.

Overall, this library provides a robust and flexible framework for implementing cryptographic primitives in C, allowing developers to easily integrate these functions into their applications while maintaining high performance and scalability.']

