To support concurrent access to the initialized arrays from multiple threads, the application uses a `List<Task>` to store all the tasks that will be created for each thread. Each task is created using the `Task.Run()` method, which allows for asynchronous execution of code. The tasks are then started using the `Task.WaitAll()` method, which waits for all tasks to complete before continuing with the rest of the program.

To ensure robustness against invalid configurations or corrupted files, the application handles potential errors during memory allocation and configuration parsing by catching any exceptions that may occur. If an exception is caught, the application will log the error message and exit gracefully.

