Next, the function gets the current Unix timestamp using `time(NULL)`. It then derives a sequence of digits from the first 10 alphanumeric characters of the original file name using a while loop that stops when it reaches the end of the string or finds a non-alphanumeric character. The derived sequence is used to generate the new file name with enhanced metadata, following the format `<directory>/<original_name>.<hash>.<timestamp>-<sequence_of_digits>.<new_extension>`.

The function checks if the generated new file name is unique within the specified directory using `stat()`. If it is not unique, the function generates a new sequence of digits and tries again until it finds a unique name. Once the new file name is unique, the function creates the new file with the generated name and extension using `fopen()` and `fclose()`.

