The `getPacket` function returns a pointer to the specified position in the dynamic array, or `NULL` if the index is out of bounds. The `freePackets` function frees all memory allocated for the dynamic array using `free`.

To minimize contention and deadlocks when accessing shared resources, this implementation uses synchronization mechanisms such as mutex locks to ensure that only one thread can access the dynamic array at a time. It also employs techniques such as lazy initialization and reference counting to reduce memory usage and improve performance.']

