The function also defines two serialization and deserialization functions `serialize_lte_ue_context` and `deserialize_lte_ue_context`, respectively, to convert the list into a binary format suitable for persistent storage and vice versa. These functions use atomic operations to optimize performance when feasible.

The code also defines a mutex variable `list_mutex` to prevent race conditions when accessing the list from multiple threads. The function uses this mutex to lock the list before modifying it, ensuring that data integrity is maintained.

To enhance usability, the code provides a modular and extendable design, allowing for easy addition of new RRC message types or enhanced logging capabilities. The function also balances the trade-off between memory overhead and I/O efficiency, prioritizing user experience and system responsiveness.

