* `<original_name>` is the base name of the original file without its extension.
* `<hash>` is a SHA-256 hash of the original file name.
* `<timestamp>` is the current Unix timestamp.
* `<sequence_of_digits>` is generated based on the first 10 characters of the original file name, excluding any non-alphanumeric characters, and should not exceed a length of 8 digits.
* `<new_extension>` is a user-defined extension that should be validated against a predefined list of allowed extensions.

